;; posterior-floor — claims whose posterior belief is below the floor (REQ-KG-006).
;;
;; Booklogic port of assets/queries/defeasible/posterior-floor.rq:
;;   SELECT ?claim ?p WHERE {
;;     ?claim a tbf:Claim ;
;;            tbf:pPosterior ?p ;
;;            tbf:supportsChapter ?chapter .
;;     FILTER (?p < 0.4)
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim tbf:pinLowConfidence true . }
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds the claim id and its p_posterior (a typed Float column), then
;; joins the claim->chapter coverage edge (the relational form of
;; tbf:supportsChapter) so only claims that support a chapter qualify -- matching
;; the .rq, which requires a tbf:supportsChapter triple. :filter applies the
;; ordered comparison ``?p < 0.4`` (the defeasible floor); the literal stays
;; unquoted so it compares against the Float column. :not negates a pinned claim
;; row joined on the same id, lowering FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim
;; tbf:pinLowConfidence true } to a safe Cozo negation: drop claims explicitly
;; pinned low-confidence (operator override). bermuda's golden is empty -- its
;; lowest projected posterior is 0.4299, above the floor.
(defquery :posterior-floor
  :find   [?claim ?p]
  :where  [[?c :claim/id ?claim]
           [?c :claim/p-posterior ?p]
           [?cc :claim-chapter/claim-id ?claim]
           [?cc :claim-chapter/chapter ?chapter]]
  :filter [[< ?p 0.4]]
  :not    [[?pin :claim/id ?claim]
           [?pin :claim/pin-low-confidence true]])
